#~
G12: a closure capturing a young object, stored in an object that is already
old, must keep the capture alive across a minor GC.

The store of the closure into the old Holder runs the write barrier, so the
Holder is in dirty_list; the capture store dirties the closure block, a
BYTE_ARY_TYPE array. ScanDirtyObject used to scan neither: it ignored
BYTE_ARY_TYPE blocks, and a holder's FUNC_PARM field descended only when the
closure block was young, which it never is (arrays are always old). So the Box,
referenced only by the capture, was not marked or promoted, and the capture
dangled once the nursery was recycled: Call() returned whatever then occupied
that address.

This started as a heap-verifier replay below programs/regression/gc_verify.
The collector fix (hardening/gcfix) made it pass interpreted, but under the
JIT it still crashed on the first call of a capturing lambda stored through a
func-ref variable (STOR_FUNC_VAR wrote the closure slot's frame offset as the
closure pointer; hardening/fix-jit-funcfield-store). With both fixed it runs
in every mode, so it is a regular test. run_vm_flag_tests.py also runs it with
OBJECK_GC_VERIFY=1; under OBJECK_GC_VERIFY=checkmark it must pass as well.

The Counts calls are load-bearing: without the calls between Store and Churn a
stale interpreter word keeps the Box alive and the loss does not show. The
counts they report differ by configuration, so they go to stderr.
~#
class ClosureCaptureOldHolder {
  function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
    bad := 0;
    holder := Holder->New();

    # promote holder: fill the nursery once
    Churn();
    Counts("after first churn");

    for(round := 0; round < 4; round += 1;) {
      Store(holder, Box->New(round * 7 + 1));
      Counts("after store");
      Churn();
      Counts("after churn");
      box := holder->Call();
      if(box = Nil) {
        bad += 1;
      }
      else if(box->GetV() <> round * 7 + 1) {
        bad += 1;
      };
    };

    if(bad = 0) {
      "PASS: closure captures survive a minor GC through an old holder"->PrintLine();
    }
    else {
      "FAIL: closure capture lost through an old holder ({$bad} bad)"->PrintLine();
      Runtime->Exit(1);
    };
  }

  function : Counts(tag : String) ~ Nil {
    count := Runtime->GetProperty("runtime.gc.minor");
    line := "{$tag} minor={$count}";
    line->ErrorLine();
  }

  function : Churn() ~ Nil {
    for(j := 0; j < 3000000; j += 1;) {
      tmp := Box->New(j);
      if(tmp->GetV() < 0) { "unreachable"->PrintLine(); };
    };
  }

  # the Box's only reference left after this returns is the closure's capture
  function : Store(holder : Holder, b : Box) ~ Nil {
    f := \() ~ Box : () => b;
    holder->Set(f);
  }
}

class Holder {
  @f : () ~ Box;

  New() {
  }

  method : public : Set(f : () ~ Box) ~ Nil {
    @f := f;
  }

  method : public : Call() ~ Box {
    return @f();
  }
}

class Box {
  @v : Int;
  @pad : Box;

  New(v : Int) {
    @v := v;
  }

  method : public : GetV() ~ Int {
    return @v;
  }
}
